            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0739" n="1573" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/885</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-22T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2981. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1691. Your 1895, Embassy 3814, November 18, 5 p.m. We doubt advisability of
                    sending letter as suggested which appears to <pb facs="0740" n="1574"
                        xml:id="pg1574"/> savor of interference in internal affairs of Holland. Our
                    recent reports of domestic situation of Holland indicate that the situation,
                    which doubtless prompted suggestion, has now passed its critical stage. We
                    assume that were present Government replaced by one which Associated Governments
                    did not recognize, we would automatically be released from compliance with
                    agreement and that it could readily be arranged informally that this be
                    understood in Holland.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
